+# smallpt playground
+
+Kevin Beason’s [smallpt](https://www.kevinbeason.com/smallpt/) C++ path tracer, compiled to WebAssembly with Emscripten. The original source and MIT license are in `vendor/`.
+
+Run `pnpm start` to serve the page (port 11222 by default). Generated WebAssembly assets are included, so no compiler is needed to use the site.
+
+Run `pnpm build` to rebuild `assets/smallpt.js` and `assets/smallpt.wasm` with Emscripten (`emcc`).
+
+`renderer/bridge.cpp` preserves smallpt’s camera, scene, and recursive radiance function and adds a progressive RGBA interface. A dedicated Web Worker traces four samples per pixel per pass and transfers frames to the canvas. Randomization changes the actual reflectance colors of the mirror and glass spheres. Quality selection restarts the render; reset restores the original colors; save downloads the canvas as PNG.
+
+The static initial preview is also output from this WebAssembly module: `node scripts/preview.cjs` writes a 256-sample PPM to `/tmp/smallpt-preview.ppm`; `python3 scripts/ppm-to-png.py` converts it to the bundled PNG. The page immediately starts a fresh client-side render.
+
+Validation: JavaScript syntax checks and execution of the compiled WebAssembly in Node. No manual browser verification.
